
══ Journal: unit tests ══

  ✓ write records entry in log
  ✓ write does NOT mutate real object
  ✓ read returns overlay value when written
  ✓ read falls through to real value when not written
  ✓ has returns true for written keys
  ✓ multiple writes to same key keep latest
  ✓ writes to different objects are independent
  ✓ writeExternal records external entries
  ✓ commit applies all writes to real objects
  ✓ clear discards all writes
  ✓ summary reports state

══ Journal: rewindTo (time travel) ══

  ✓ rewindTo rebuilds overlay
  ✓ rewindTo(0) clears overlay
  ✓ rewind then write creates new branch
  ✓ undefined values are handled correctly

══ Debug mode: journal integration ══

  ✓ bracket writes go to journal in debug mode
  ✓ bracket reads see journal overlay
  ✓ method calls are logged as side effects
  ✓ commit applies journal writes to real state
  ✓ discard leaves real state unchanged
  ✓ multiple writes accumulate in journal
  ✓ onCommit callback receives result

══ Debug mode: time travel ══

  ✓ rewindTo restores state and notifies host

